<h1>Justin Jefferson's Ankle Sprain: <em>A Slow Start Gets Slower</em></h1>
<div class="meta-row">
<span>📖 5 min read</span>
<span>🏈 Football</span>
<span>⚠️ Vikings · Ankle</span>
</div>
<p class="dek">Justin Jefferson sprained his left ankle in the first quarter of Minnesota's Week 3 win over Tampa Bay and sat out Week 4, leaving the Vikings with almost no snaps of Jefferson and new quarterback Kyler Murray on the field together. Jefferson's 2020 combine was a quiet surprise: a 4.43 forty from a receiver no one expected to run that fast. Here is the profile behind one of the league's best route runners.</p>
</div><div class="content">
<div class="toc">
<div class="toc-label">In This Article</div>
