<h2 id="outlook">Minnesota Without Its Top Target</h2>
<p>With Jefferson out, Jordan Addison stepped into the lead role, catching five passes for 90 yards and a touchdown after Jefferson left Tampa. Minnesota's three-receiver sets rely on Addison, Jauan Jennings and either Myles Price or Tai Felton. Jefferson had led the NFL in receiving yards per game from 2020 through 2024, and the offense Murray was brought in to run is built around his presence.</p>
<div class="callout">
<strong>Reading the Injury</strong>
  A sprained ankle that the coaching staff calls mild is usually a short-term issue, and Jefferson has been unusually durable, playing every game in five of his six full seasons. The bigger question for Minnesota is not this ankle but whether Jefferson and Murray can build rhythm once both are healthy at the same time.
</div>
